CORE
main.c
--32 --unwind 2 --rounds 3 --por --array-rf-bytes --allow-pointer-unsoundness
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
--
Two threads store different members of the same element of an array of structs at a computed index. Each element used to publish all its members under i == k, the untouched ones with this thread stale values, so one store reset the other. Only the stored member is published now. Fails on a binary without the fix.
